---
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import heroImage from "../assets/images/hero-home.avif";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  heroImage={heroImage}
  heroImageAlt="Two overlapping circles of personal space, drawn as gold rings on a cream ground, in a two-ink risograph print"
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    You will run a field method on your own life: notice who gets how much
    room, who yields to whom, and what a space is silently asking of the
    people in it. Each week hands you a lens — civil inattention, proxemics,
    third places, the informal rules of a shared kitchen or a shared
    codebase — and a short, specific task to try it on a real room you
    already spend time in. You walk out with a working diagnostic method,
    a written protocol you have tested on a group you actually belong to,
    and a critique-and-redesign of one space that currently gets
    coexistence wrong.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone about to share a home, a workplace, a studio or a lab bench with
    people they did not choose — which is to say, almost everyone after
    school. No prior social-science background is assumed; you need only a
    room with more than one person in it and a willingness to watch it
    closely instead of just living in it. It is not group-therapy or a
    personality inventory: what you hand in is a diagnosis, a protocol, or
    a redesign, and it is marked as one.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>The weekly schedule and what happens in each teaching session.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>What is marked, what it is worth, and when it is due.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course and how to reach them.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
